  "authenticity": {
    "note": "Fixed ed25519 material so an implementation in ANY language can be measured without generating keys and without agreeing with itself. Only PUBLIC material is stored: a public key, documents, and signatures. No private key is here and none is needed — verification is the operation under test. Regenerate by signing the base document with a fresh key and replacing publicKeyPem, fingerprint and every signature. The registry is the INSTALLATION's trust store: it is built from registeredPublisherId and registeredFingerprint, never from the publisher the document under test claims to be — deriving it from the document would make the registry agree with every forgery that renames itself.",
